From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Harini Pavithra Elangovan <helangov@qti.qualcomm.com>
Date: Mon, 19 May 2026 15:00:00 +0530
Subject: [PATCH] wpaCtrlEvents: add ERROR log in s_apStationAssocFailure

Add SAH_TRACEZ_ERROR log in s_apStationAssocFailure() which is the
first entry point in pwhm when it receives AP-STA-POSSIBLE-PSK-MISMATCH
or CTRL-EVENT-SAE-UNKNOWN-PASSWORD-IDENTIFIER from hostapd via wpa_ctrl.

This confirms pwhm received and processed the event. The log is at
ERROR level to ensure visibility without requiring INFO-level logging.

Note: These events are only triggered in prplmesh/beerocks setup.
The ath12k driver handles the 4-way handshake in firmware and does
not expose these events to hostapd in standalone pwhm setup.

Signed-off-by: Harini Pavithra Elangovan <helangov@qti.qualcomm.com>
---
 src/nl80211/wld_wpaCtrl_events.c | 4 +++-
 1 file changed, 3 insertions(+), 1 deletion(-)

--- a/src/nl80211/wld_wpaCtrl_events.c
+++ b/src/nl80211/wld_wpaCtrl_events.c
@@ -337,10 +337,12 @@ static void s_apStationAssocFailure(wld_wpaCtrlInterface_t* pInterface, char* e
-static void s_apStationAssocFailure(wld_wpaCtrlInterface_t* pInterface, char* event _UNUSED, char* params) {
+static void s_apStationAssocFailure(wld_wpaCtrlInterface_t* pInterface, char* event, char* params) {
     //Example: AP-STA-POSSIBLE-PSK-MISMATCH xx:xx:xx:xx:xx:xx
     //Example: AP-STA-POSSIBLE-PSK-MISMATCH xx:xx:xx:xx:xx:xx status=x reason=x
     //Example: CTRL-EVENT-SAE-UNKNOWN-PASSWORD-IDENTIFIER xx:xx:xx:xx:xx:xx
     char buf[SWL_MAC_CHAR_LEN] = {0};
     swl_macBin_t bStationMac;
 
+    SAH_TRACEZ_ERROR(ME, "%s: pwhm received wpaCtrlEvent: %s %s", pInterface->name, event, params);
+
     memcpy(buf, params, SWL_MAC_CHAR_LEN - 1);
     bool ret = swl_mac_charToBin(&bStationMac, (swl_macChar_t*) buf);
     ASSERT_TRUE(ret, , ME, "fail to convert mac address to binary");
